        "zoom": [
          1,
          1.08
        ]
      },
      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Los dioses llevaron a Baldr hasta Hringhorni, su gran barco, pero ni todos juntos lograban echarlo al mar.",
          "en": "The gods carried Baldr to Hringhorni, his great ship, but not even all of them together could push it into the sea."
        },
        {
          "es": "Llamaron a la giganta Hyrrokkin, que llegó montada en un lobo, y de un solo empujón lanzó el barco al agua.",
          "en": "They called the giantess Hyrrokkin, who arrived riding a wolf, and with a single shove she sent the ship into the water."
        },
        {
          "es": "Nanna, la esposa de Baldr, murió de pena, y la pusieron a su lado en la pira.",
          "en": "Nanna, Baldr's wife, died of grief, and they laid her beside him on the pyre."
        },
        {
          "es": "Odín dejó sobre la pira su anillo Draupnir, y se inclinó para susurrarle algo al oído a su hijo.",
          "en": "Odin placed his ring Draupnir on the pyre, and leaned down to whisper something in his son's ear."
        },
        {
          "es": "Nadie ha sabido nunca qué le dijo. Y el barco, ardiendo, se alejó mar adentro.",
          "en": "No one has ever known what he said. And the ship, burning, drifted out to sea."
        }
      ],
